    "rawResponseText": "If **affiliation flexibility** is the priority for a hotel conversion in Europe, owners should look first at **soft brands** and **collection brands** that combine lighter standards with strong distribution and loyalty access.[11][12][17]\n\nThe strongest options highlighted in the results are:\n\n- **Marriott Autograph Collection** — a well-known soft brand for independent hotels that want to keep their identity while joining Marriott’s system.[2][3][8][18]\n- **Marriott Tribute Portfolio** — another Marriott soft brand gaining traction for conversions and flexible affiliation.[2][3]\n- **Marriott Luxury Collection** — suited to upscale/luxury assets seeking softer conversion requirements.[2][3]\n- **Hilton Curio Collection** — cited as a classic soft-brand example for independent hotels seeking more flexibility.[14][18]\n- **Accor MGallery** — a soft-brand option aimed at hotels wanting individuality with group support.[8]\n- **Accor Handwritten Collection** — explicitly designed for independent hotel owners and described as flexible, with many likely conversion projects.[9]\n- **IHG Vignette Collection** — positioned as a flexible luxury/lifestyle soft brand for independents.[2][5]\n- **IHG voco hotels** — a premium conversion-friendly soft brand with flexible standards.[5]\n- **IHG Garner** — especially relevant for lower-midscale conversions because of its flexible design standards and rapid conversion model.[5]\n- **IHG Ruby** — designed for urban lifestyle and adaptive reuse/conversion projects, including in major European cities.[5]\n- **Preferred Hotels & Resorts** and **The Leading Hotels of the World** — voluntary collection-style affiliations that preserve more independence than many corporate soft brands.[12][15]\n- **Marriott Series by Marriott** — a newer flexible collection for conversion-focused, budget-conscious hotels in Europe.[7]\n\nIn practical terms, the results suggest a useful split:\n\n- **Corporate soft brands**: **Autograph, Tribute, Curio, MGallery, Vignette, voco, Handwritten Collection**.[2][5][9][14][18]\n- **Voluntary collections / affiliation networks**: **Preferred Hotels & Resorts, The Leading Hotels of the World**.[12][15]\n\nIf the owner’s main goal is **maximum flexibility with the least identity loss**, the voluntary collections are usually the most flexible.[15] If the goal is **still flexible but with stronger chain distribution and loyalty power**, the corporate soft brands are the better fit.[11][12][17]\n\nFor **Europe specifically**, the results most strongly point to **Marriott’s soft brands, IHG’s conversion-friendly brands, and Accor’s flexible collection brands** as the most relevant choices for conversions.[2][3][5][7][9]",
